artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $k$ be a field. A connected graded $k$-algebra $A=\bigoplus_{n\geq 0}A_n$ with $A_0=k$ and each $A_n$ finite-dimensional over $k$ is called Artin–Schelter regular (AS-regular) of dimension $d$ if it satisfies:

(i) $A$ has finite global dimension $d<\infty$;
(ii) $A$ has finite Gelfand–Kirillov dimension, i.e., there is a constant $c$ such that $\dim_k(A_0\oplus A_1\oplus\cdots\oplus A_n)\leq c\,n^c$ for all $n\geq 1$;
(iii) $A$ is Gorenstein, meaning $\operatorname{Ext}^i_A(k,A)=0$ for $i\neq d$ and $\operatorname{Ext}^d_A(k,A)\cong k$ (up to a graded shift), where $k$ is the trivial graded left $A$-module $A/A_{\geq 1}$.

Question: Must every Artin–Schelter regular algebra $A$ be noetherian (i.e., must every left ideal and every right ideal of $A$ be finitely generated)?

